<h1>Terms of supply</h1>

<p>Unless a separate written agreement is in place, all purchase orders issued by Meridian Castings Limited are subject to the terms summarised below. The full terms are issued with each purchase order and take precedence over any conflicting terms printed on a supplier's order acknowledgement or invoice.</p>

<p>Standard payment terms are sixty days from the end of the month of invoice, provided the invoice matches an accepted delivery against a valid purchase order number. Goods supplied for use in production must be accompanied by a certificate of conformity referencing the relevant specification, and where a specification calls for a named process, such as heat treatment or plating to a customer standard, the supplier must hold current approval for that process.</p>

<p>Suppliers are expected to notify Meridian Castings promptly of any change that could affect fitness for purpose, including a change of manufacturing location, sub-tier supplier, or material source. Non-conforming deliveries are handled under our standard quality process; see <a href="/quality">quality management</a> for how this connects to our own inspection records.</p>

<p>New suppliers should first complete the steps described under <a href="/suppliers/onboarding">supplier onboarding</a>. For questions about a specific purchase order, use our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
